<h3>1:12:07 — Reason: go back to the `throws` heading, first point</h3>
<p>Scratch-check the throws heading, first point: in our program if there is a chance / possibility of raising a checked exception, compulsory we should handle, otherwise the code won’t compile.</p>
<p>Exception is checked or unchecked? Checked. You are throwing a checked exception → there is a chance of raising a checked exception → compiler asks where you are handling → unreported exception `java.lang.Exception` must be caught or declared to be thrown.</p>
<p>Error is checked or unchecked? Unchecked. Remember. Compiler always talks about only checked. Chance of raising unchecked → compiler never objects → no compile-time error.</p>
<p>But at runtime we are throwing Error and there is no catch. Default exception handler terminates the program abnormally, printing:</p>
<p>Exception in thread &quot;main&quot; java.lang.Error
        at Test.main(...)</p>
<p>First one = checked exception problem (CE). Second = unchecked, no CE, but at runtime the error comes.</p>
<pre class='code'>class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        throw new Exception();
        // CE: unreported exception java.lang.Exception
        //     must be caught or declared to be thrown
    }
}
class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        throw new Error();
    }
}
// javac: OK
// java Test:
// Exception in thread &quot;main&quot; java.lang.Error
//         at Test.main(Test.java:3)</pre>
<p>If you do handle the checked Exception, both the compiler and the “must handle checked” rule are satisfied — he does not dwell on these two fixes, but they are the two ways from the start of the video:</p>
<pre class='code'>class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        throw new Exception();
        // compiles; then JVM → abnormal termination if it actually throws
    }
}
class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            throw new Exception();
        } catch (Exception e) {
        }
        // compiles; handled → normal termination
    }
}</pre>
