<pre class='code'>class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            System.out.println(&quot;hello&quot;);
        } catch (InterruptedException e) {
        }
        // CE: exception java.lang.InterruptedException is never thrown
        //     in body of corresponding try statement
    }
}</pre>
<p>Example 5 — `Error` (unchecked):</p>
<pre class='code'>class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            System.out.println(&quot;hello&quot;);
        } catch (Error e) {
        }
    }
}
// compiles; prints hello</pre>
<p>Total five examples. Among these five: how many compile, how many won’t? Most dangerous concept.</p>
<h3>1:22:52 — Quiz with fake hints (he is checking whether you know)</h3>
